  "wikipedia": {
    "title": "Alkaid",
    "description": "Star in the constellation Ursa Major",
    "summary": "Alkaid, also called Eta Ursae Majoris, is a star in the constellation of Ursa Major. It is the easternmost star in the Big Dipper asterism. However, unlike most stars of the Big Dipper, it is not a member of the Ursa Major moving group. With an apparent visual magnitude of +1.86, it is the third-brightest star in the constellation and one of the brightest stars in the night sky.",
    "intro": "Alkaid , also called Eta Ursae Majoris (Latinised from η Ursae Majoris, abbreviated Eta UMa, η UMa), is a star in the constellation of Ursa Major. It is the easternmost star in the Big Dipper (or Plough) asterism. However, unlike most stars of the Big Dipper, it is not a member of the Ursa Major moving group. With an apparent visual magnitude of +1.86, it is the third-brightest star in the constellation and one of the brightest stars in the night sky.",
    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alkaid",
